@startuml seq-stdin-typed-open
'' PlantUML over Mermaid: this is a four-participant, three-phase hand-off (drain/spill → socket →
'' registry-mediated open) whose whole point is WHERE facts live at each step — a sequence diagram with
'' phase dividers and per-concept colors states that precisely. Amber = IPC seams, slate = main-process
'' services, teal = renderer, brown = filesystem/terminal.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title ADR-0036 — <latex>\texttt{git\ diff\ |\ vv\ -t\ diff}</latex> : a piped document with an explicit type

participant "terminal\n(git diff | …)" as Term FS_TINT
participant "vv-open.mjs\n(GUI client)" as Client IPC_TINT
participant "daemon socket\n+ startup/socket-specs" as Daemon MAIN_TINT
participant "doc-overrides\nregistry (main)" as Reg DATASCRIPT_TINT
participant "service.cljs\nsend-content!" as Svc MAIN_TINT
participant "renderer\n(:content/received)" as R RENDERER_TINT

== drain + spill (client side — the resident daemon cannot see this terminal's pipe) ==
Term -> Client : piped bytes … EOF
activate Client
Client -> Client : scan argv: files=[], types=["diff"]
Client -> Term : spill → $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vinary-viewer/\nstdin/<uuid>/stdin  (0700/0600)
note right of Client #F4F1E1: zero piped bytes ⇒ NO stdin document\n(types shift to the named files)

== the v2 open message (additive; a legacy daemon ignores the new fields) ==
Client -> Daemon : {args:[…/stdin], types:["diff"],\nstdinIndex:0, cwd:"/work/repo", instanceId}
deactivate Client
activate Daemon
Daemon -> Daemon : socket-specs → resolve-specs\n(vinary.file-type — the ONE resolver)
alt unknown type / mispaired types
  Daemon --> Client : {"ok":false,"error":"vv: unknown type '…'"}
  note right of Client #FBE9E7: printed on the invoking terminal,\nspill unlinked, exit 1
else valid specs
  Daemon -> Reg : register! path {:kind "diff"\n:stdin? true :cwd "/work/repo"}
  Daemon -> R : vv:open-files {paths:[…/stdin]}\n(the UNCHANGED renderer pipeline)
end
deactivate Daemon

== every send consults the registry (override survives Reload / facet nav / watcher refreshes) ==
R -> Svc : vv:open "…/stdin"
activate Svc
Svc -> Reg : effective-kind → "diff"\nstdin-doc? → skip tree + watcher
Svc -> Svc : openLocal(path, "diff")\n(explicit kind ⇒ no classify, no sniff)
Svc --> R : vv:content {kind:"diff", text, stdin:true,\nbaseDir:"/work/repo", meta{size}}
deactivate Svc
R -> R : :diff/render → unified view;\nstdin flag ⇒ no Recent-MRU entry
note over Reg, R #EEE6EF: Settings ▸ File Type later re-types the SAME path:\nvv:set-file-type → set-type! (stdin facts survive) → re-send.\nSide-by-side enrichment resolves a/… b/… against baseDir\n(the repo the diff was generated in).

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| terminal / filesystem |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| IPC seam (client · socket · channels) |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| main-process services |
  |<#A45BAD>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| doc-overrides registry (per-path facts) |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| renderer |
  The registry is why the type can never silently revert: send-content!
  consults it on EVERY send, including watcher live-refreshes.
endlegend
@enduml
